language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Each different letter stands for a different digit, so that the sum of the sixteen words listed in the puzzle equals ALL WOOL.
find C, H, E, S, A, B, O, W, P, L : int(0..9)

such that
$ each different letter stands for a different digit
allDiff([C, H, E, S, A, B, O, W, P, L]),
$ the words above the line add up to ALL WOOL, with the letters read as digits in each place
((10000*C + 1000*H + 100*E + 10*S + S) + (1000*C + 100*A + 10*S + H) + (100000*B + 10000*O + 1000*W + 100*W + 10*O + W) + (10000*C + 1000*H + 100*O + 10*P + S) + (100000*A + 10000*L + 1000*S + 100*O + 10*P + S) + (1000000*P + 100000*A + 10000*L + 1000*E + 100*A + 10*L + E) + (1000*C + 100*O + 10*O + L) + (1000*B + 100*A + 10*S + S) + (1000*H + 100*O + 10*P + S) + (1000*A + 100*L + 10*E + S) + (1000*H + 100*O + 10*E + S) + (100000*A + 10000*P + 1000*P + 100*L + 10*E + S) + (1000*C + 100*O + 10*W + S) + (100000*C + 10000*H + 1000*E + 100*E + 10*S + E) + (100000*C + 10000*H + 1000*S + 100*O + 10*A + P) + (10000*S + 1000*H + 100*E + 10*E + P)) = (1000000*A + 100000*L + 10000*L + 1000*W + 100*O + 10*O + L)
